81 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(This system provides immediate hazard notifications through both visual and auditory  alerts. The optical alarm uses a high-intensity LED beacon or strobe light to ensure visibility, while the  acoustic alarm employs a loud buzzer or siren to grab attention. These alarms are activated upon  detection of hazardous conditions such as gas leaks, overpressure, or extreme temperatures, ensuring  prompt response and enhanced safety.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

82 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Supplementary PT100 Sensor)/E(Supplementary PT100 Sensor)/Pg 10 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

83 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 32 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

84 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(The PT100 sensor is a precision temperature sensor that provides additional temperature  monitoring within the test chamber. It offers accurate readings and quick response times, ensuring that  temperature variations are detected and managed effectively, thus maintaining the integrity of the  testing environment and preventing overheating or other temperature-related issues.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

85 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Reversible Overpressure Valve)/E(Reversible Overpressure Valve)/Pg 10 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

86 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 32 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

87 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(This valve is designed to manage pressure changes safely within the chamber. It  automatically releases excess pressure, preventing potential damage to the chamber or hazardous  situations. The valve can reset itself after activation, ensuring continuous protection without the need for  manual intervention.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

