<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Additional Door Locks)/E(Additional Door Locks)/Pg 10 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

90 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Enhanced security is provided through additional door locks, which  ensure that the chamber remains sealed during operation. These locks prevent  unauthorized access and maintain a controlled environment, which is crucial for the  accuracy and safety of the tests being conducted.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

91 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Battery Gas Monitoring)/E(Battery Gas Monitoring)/Pg 10 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

92 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 32 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

93 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Continuous monitoring of hydrogen \(H2\) and carbon monoxide \(CO\)  levels is critical in battery testing environments. This system uses advanced sensors  to detect the presence of these gases, which can be indicative of potentially  dangerous conditions. Immediate alerts are provided if gas levels exceed safe  thresholds, allowing for prompt corrective action.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

94 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Compressed Air or GN2 Washing)/E(Compressed Air or GN2 Washing)/Pg 10 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

95 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 32 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

96 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(This feature maintains a safe atmosphere within the chamber by using  compressed air or gaseous nitrogen \(GN2\) to purge and clean the internal  environment. This process helps to remove any contaminants or hazardous gases,  ensuring a controlled and safe testing space.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

