169 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(EUCAR Hazard Levels)/E(EUCAR Hazard Levels)/Pg 13 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

170 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(These levels help assess the danger associated with handling batteries. They are defined by the European Council for Automotive R&D \(EUCAR\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

171 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(The levels range from 0 to 7, with increasing severity:)/Pg 13 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

172 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Level 0: No effect, no loss of functionality.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

173 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Level 1: Passive protection activated; cell reversibly damaged.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

174 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Level 2: Cell damaged irreversibly; replacement needed.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

175 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Level 3: Leakage, loss of mass < 50% \(no fire or explosion\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

176 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Level 4: Leakage, loss of mass > 50% \(no fire or explosion\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

177 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Level 5: Fire or flame \(no rupture or explosion\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

178 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Level 6: Rupture \(no explosion, but flying parts\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

179 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Level 7: Explosion \(disintegration of the cell\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

180 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Based on your Offered test chamber hazard level  it will applicable. Battery Test Chambers included with battery safety testing features equipped to handle up to hazard level 7:)/Pg 13 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

