endobj

332 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(The Table Top Climatic Test Chamber boasts extensive data storage capabilities, allowing for the retention of test data for up to 100 days. Additionally, users have the ability to create and save up to 100 test profiles, streamlining the setup process and facilitating efficient testing procedures.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

333 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Certainly, our HMI provides comprehensive access level password protection. End-users will have their login IDs with customizable permissions based on different levels. The system allows for the creation of up to 12 levels of passwords, each with its specific permissions.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

334 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Furthermore, users with appropriate access levels can edit high/low alarm limits directly through the HMI interface. This functionality ensures that users can tailor alarm settings to their specific requirements without compromising security or ease of use.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

335 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 41 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

336 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 41 0 R/Pg 19 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

337 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Humidity System)/E(Humidity System)/Pg 19 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

338 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Our Climatic only for ETC model  test chamber is equipped with an immersion heater-based boiler tank. The chamber includes a 15-20 liter inbuilt water storage tank, which is connected to the boiler tank through a water solenoid valve. The system features an automated water filling system with an electrical water level sensor that maintains the water level in the boiler tank. This ensures efficient and continuous humidity control inside the test chamber.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

339 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Dehumidification System)/E(Dehumidification System)/Pg 19 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

340 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(The dehumidification system is controlled via PLC logic. It operates through a de-humidity solenoid valve, integrated with the refrigeration system. The cooling coil contains a refrigeration cold tube that absorbs moisture from the chamber's air. The system monitors the cold tube temperature through the PLC. When dehumidification is required, the cold tube captures the moisture, freezes it into water particles, and drains the condensed water, effectively reducing the chamber's internal humidity.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

341 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(Certification)/E(Certification)/Pg 19 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

